Implement a Config class responsible for reading "Watch\watch-config.txt" as a simple key=value text file, ignoring comments and blank lines, and normalizing keys exactly as done in 0.4.0 so that existing field configurations remain valid without modification. The loader should open the configuration file using regular file access semantics and parse each line into a dictionary of strongly typed properties, including LogPath, window settings, dashboard port, and other tunables described in the PRD. When loading values, validate ranges and types, and for any invalid or out-of-range entry, log a clear message to the console and rewrite the configuration file to a corrected default value, preserving the PRD’s self-correcting behavior. In report mode, Config must not write back LogPath, whereas in dashboard mode, a Start action may update LogPath to reflect the last opened log as in 0.4.x. Implement precedence so that CLI arguments always override the configuration file when both are present, matching the existing semantics described in the PRD.
```csharp
public sealed class WatchConfig
{
 public string? LogPath { get; set; }
 public int DashboardPort { get; set; }
 // other keys...

 public static WatchConfig Load(string path)
 {
 var config = new WatchConfig();
 foreach (var line in File.ReadLines(path))
 {
 if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(line) || line.TrimStart().StartsWith("#"))
 continue;
 var parts = line.Split('=', 2);
 if (parts.Length != 2) continue;
 var key = parts.Trim();
 var value = parts.Trim();
 // parse and validate keys
 }
 // self-correction pass that rewrites invalid entries
 return config;
 }
}
